# EMG-Controlled Adaptive Gripper — CNL Spec
# Demo 1: An SNN reads forearm EMG, classifies grip intent, and drives
# a gripper with spiking motor commands that adapt via STDP.

The network MUST operate WITH timestep of 1 ms

The network MUST contain an excitatory sensory population of 1 neurons
The network MUST contain an excitatory interneuron population of 60 neurons
The network MUST contain an excitatory motor population of 1 neurons

# Sensory population fires when EMG amplitude exceeds detection threshold
The sensory population MUST fire ONLY IF membrane potential exceeds 0.8

# Interneuron separates intent detection from final gripper actuation
The interneuron population MUST fire ONLY IF membrane potential exceeds 0.55

# Motor population fires when activation exceeds grip command threshold
The motor population MUST emit a spike ONLY IF membrane potential exceeds 0.6

# Refractory periods prevent runaway firing
The sensory population MUST NOT fire DURING the refractory period of 0.002 seconds
The motor population MUST NOT fire DURING the refractory period of 0.003 seconds

# Membrane dynamics with fast time constants for responsive control
The sensory population membrane potential MUST decay WITH time constant of 0.01 seconds
The motor population membrane potential MUST decay WITH time constant of 0.02 seconds

# Adaptive gripper topology uses an intermediate intent population
The sensory population MUST project to interneuron population
The interneuron population MUST project to motor population
The sensory population MUST project to motor population

The connection from sensory population to interneuron population MUST have WITH synaptic weight of 1.5
The connection from interneuron population to motor population MUST have WITH synaptic weight of 1.2
The connection from sensory population to motor population MUST have WITH synaptic weight of 0.5

# STDP: synapse strengthens when grip correlates with EMG intent
The connection from sensory population to interneuron population MUST adapt WITH STDP learning rate of 0.0001

# STDP: synapse weakens for anti-causal timing
The connection from sensory population to interneuron population MUST weaken IF post fires before pre WITHIN 20 ms

# Weight bounds prevent runaway excitation or silencing
A synapse MUST NOT have weights exceeding 3.0
A synapse MUST NOT have weights below 0.1
